From 4c5b906463419b1f80794922172eeefa3011895b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:03:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: GS downloads stall instead of fabricating data; header
 cleanups

- VIF1 -> memory download stops at an empty GS FIFO with MADR/QWC/STR
  intact (CHCR reads keep STR) and resumes after the next GIF work, instead
  of writing zeros and completing (review 55 G1; VIF1_STAT.FDR is still
  not required).
- Under paraLLEl-GS a partial transfer tail takes one whole qword from its
  FIFO, so a PSMCT24 download no longer leaves a stale qword for the next
  one; the SDK image stubs size PSMCT24 at 3 bytes per pixel (G3).
- Removed the never-called IopHost::invokeGuestFunction and the unused
  VU1 store ring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
